summary: 'The founder approved starting the M1.1 contract reservations (every value listed in spec v3.9 §4.11 and §19.1 M1.1; clientApiId expected to move once now) and the first M1.4 slice: real hello negotiation, serverSig plus device-key mutual auth, an authenticated dispatch skeleton, a real status verb, and auth events in the kernel log. Root and device registration go behind a RootAuthority seam, because hardware root keys (M1.3) are blocked on the founder''s provisioning profile. Both pass through reviewer plus Aegis. The bypass-mode question was not answered, so the spec default stands: no bypass run mode (manual/ask/auto-edits only), revisitable.'
